<title>ITALY: CYCLING-TIRRENO-ADRIATICO SIX STAGE PLACINGS.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-TIRRENO-ADRIATICO SIX STAGE PLACINGS.</headline>
<dateline>MONTEGRANARO, Italy 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>leading placings in</p>
<p>the 160-km sixth stage of the Tirreno-Adriatico cycle race from</p>
<p>Monte Urano on Tuesday (Italians unless stated)</p>
<p>1. Dimitry Konyshev (Russia) 3 hours 57 minutes 38 seconds</p>
<p>2. Roberto Petito			 12 seconds behind</p>
<p>3. Kai Hundertmark (Germany)</p>
<p>4. Francesco Casagrande</p>
<p>5. Michele Bartoli</p>
<p>6. Kevin Livingston (United States)</p>
<p>7. Stefano Della Santa</p>
<p>8. Massimiliano Gentili</p>
<p>9. Rolf Aldag (Germany)</p>
<p>10.Beat Zberg (Switzerland)	   all same time</p>
<p>Leading overall standings:</p>
<p> 1. Petito	 24 hours 27 minutes 21 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Gianluca Pianegonda		   9 seconds behind</p>
<p> 3. Zberg				    15</p>
<p> 4. Gentili				  26</p>
<p> 5. Davide Casarotto		     27</p>
<p> 6. Vassily Davidenko		    51</p>
<p> 7. Luc Leblanc (France)		 57</p>
<p> 8. Massimo Donati		     1:28</p>
</text>
